WEBVTT

00:00:00.455 --> 00:00:02.957
Ordinal variables have a meaningful order.

00:00:02.957 --> 00:00:07.547
Emergent is more severe than urgent, and urgent is more severe than non-urgent.

00:00:07.547 --> 00:00:10.932
But the distance between those levels is not necessarily equal.

00:00:10.932 --> 00:00:15.717
That means numeric codes can preserve rank while still requiring caution.

00:00:15.717 --> 00:00:22.362
Medians, percentiles, and ordered displays often respect the structure better than treating the values as

00:00:22.362 --> 00:00:23.897
ordinary continuous numbers.

00:00:23.897 --> 00:00:29.747
The easiest way to classify a variable is to ask what statements are meaningful in the real world.

00:00:29.747 --> 00:00:34.562
Can values only be different, can they be ordered, are differences meaningful, and does zero mean absence?

00:00:34.562 --> 00:00:41.522
Those questions are more reliable than looking at whether the software stores the column as an integer or

00:00:41.522 --> 00:00:42.640
floating-point number.
